# Calculating the thirtieth Fibonacci number
#
# Each Fibonacci number is the sum of the two before it, starting from 0 and
# 1. Two base cases and a recursive backward rule (<=) define the sequence,
# and a forward rule asks for the thirtieth value: 832040. It shows recursion
# through backward rules and arithmetic built-ins.

@prefix math: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/math#> .
@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eyepl/examples/fibonacci#> .

# The first two numbers, true without any condition.
{
    (0) :fib 0
} <= true .

{
    (1) :fib 1
} <= true .

# Beyond them, fib(n) = fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2).
{
    (?n) :fib ?f
} <= {
    ?n math:greaterThan 1 .
    (?n 1) math:difference ?previous .
    (?n 2) math:difference ?earlier .
    (?previous) :fib ?a .
    (?earlier) :fib ?b .
    (?a ?b) math:sum ?f .
} .

# The question: the thirtieth Fibonacci number.
{
    (30) :fib ?value
} => {
    :query :fib ?value
} .
